  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Warm Workbench",
    "overview": "A familiar track-list tool, refined: pine-tinted neutral grounds stacked in three quiet steps, white cards that lift one soft level off the page, and a single pine accent that carries everything the user acts on: the primary action, the play button, the waveform itself, the trim grips, the focus ring. The one owned moment is the trim: a full-width bar waveform with a pine kept region, ends washed back toward the card, and pill grips that show a live time bubble while dragged.\n\nDensity is calm and generous: one centred column, large covers, the kept duration set as the headline number of each card. Everything else (labels, secondary text, controls at rest) recedes into faintly green greys so the pine reads as \"this is what you can touch or what you keep\". Dark mode is a mirror on deep pine-tinted charcoal, not an inversion: the same three-step ground, the pine lifted to a lighter tone that carries dark text.\n\nRejected by the product brief and absent from the build: glass, decorative gradients, skeuomorphic tape or cassette costume, the stock grey shadcn utility look.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Three-step pine-tinted ground: page, chrome bars, white cards.",
      "One pine accent for actions, the waveform, the kept region and focus.",
      "Rounded variable sans (Nunito) with tabular figures everywhere.",
      "Soft one-level shadow on cards, covers, grips and the paste field; no other elevation.",
      "Pills for actions and handles; generous rounding on containers.",
      "Motion only where it confirms state: waveform grow-in, grip settle; all gated on reduced motion."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Pine Rule",
        "body": "Pine marks what the user acts on or keeps, and nothing else. No pine headings, no pine decoration, no second accent hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Three Grounds Rule",
        "body": "Depth comes from the ground stack: page (`background`), chrome bars (`chrome`), cards (`card`). A new surface picks one of the three; it does not invent a fourth tint.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The On-Pine Rule",
        "body": "Text and icons on a pine fill use `primary-foreground`, in both themes; it is white on the light-mode pine and deep pine ink on the dark-mode pine. Never hard-code either.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Time Rule",
        "body": "`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` is set on `body`; every time, count and percentage inherits it so digits never jitter while dragging or playing.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Family Rule",
        "body": "Nunito Variable for everything. Weight 600 is the ceiling; emphasis comes from size, not heavier weights.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Lift Rule",
        "body": "One shadow level only. Nothing stacks above a card except the grip and the time bubble, and neither gets a stronger shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do route every colour through the CSS custom properties in `src/index.css`; both themes are defined there and components never hard-code a theme.",
      "Do keep pine for actions, the waveform, the kept region, checked state and focus only.",
      "Do use `shadow-card` for anything that lifts off the ground, and nothing stronger.",
      "Do shape pressable single objects (primary action, play, grips, bubbles) as full pills.",
      "Do put text on pine in `primary-foreground`, which resolves to white in light mode and deep pine ink in dark mode.",
      "Do gate every animation behind `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`, using `cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)`.",
      "Do read waveform colours from the CSS variables at runtime and recolour on scheme change, as the track card does."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add glass, backdrop blur or decorative gradients.",
      "Don't dress the app as a tape or cassette.",
      "Don't introduce a second accent hue or a fourth ground tint.",
      "Don't fall back to the stock grey shadcn look (ring-outlined cards, neutral-grey base) for new surfaces.",
      "Don't add a second display face; Nunito Variable carries every role."
    ]
  }
}
